Hey Adam,

Don't know if you figured this out already or not, but was just looking at some of the logdensity options in JAGS: I think maybe the issue with  "log.lik.AMMA[tt,ii,jj]<- logdensity.cat <http://logdensity.cat/>(detect.AMMA[tt,ii,jj],pi.AMMA[tt,ii,jj,],z.AMMA[tt+1,ii])"
is that the categorical distribution only has one argument (pi,or the set of probabilities), and so the logdensity.cat <http://logdensity.cat> should only have two arguments: the data being considered, and the set of probabilities associated with the categorical outcome.

Cheers,

John

