MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Should have done the proper reading/simulation first. For whatever it is worth, It appears that the marginal form of the log posterior density and the variance in the marginal form of the log-likelihood is more appropriate (is used by Broms et al 2016, although Hooten and Hobbs appear to use a conditional formlation), and using both marginal and conditional formulations (one for calculating derivations associated with z[i], one for estimating the log posterior density) easy enough to do within a single model.  Also, the final paragraph above appears embarrassingly incorrect: the conditional formulation not only tends to produce far lower estimates of pwaic, but also a much greater lpd estimate.

