OK, I've figured it out. The problem was indeed the empty "final columns" for individuals never recaptured. To resolve it I've stacked the recapture arrays next to each other for each release state, giving a single column at the end for individuals never recaptured, for each release state. Most of the code is the same as the original post, just with a few index changes and code to reformat the recapture array and probability array from four dimensions to three. It's just run successfully (and much quicker than the state space formulation with individual capture histories).

